    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After one of the heaviest rainy seasons in three decades, an extreme weather event pushed the Euphrates river past its limits. Dam operations and heavy rainfall breached protective embankments, causing widespread flooding. Rescuers offered a lifeline with a state-led rescue mission, while the leader bearing witness to the suffering visited the flood zones. Innocent lives were lost, the youngest victims of a natural trial, but a bilateral water management agreement with the upstream country promised to ease the burden, offering a path toward recovery and trust.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "how-4",
