      ],
      "fit": 0.75
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "An unprecedented natural trial caused flooding of populated areas in Deir Ezzor and Raqqa. The breach of flood defenses led to the shattering of homes and livelihoods, with the youngest victims suffering fatalities from drowning. In response, the head of state assessing the damage coordinated a rescue operation, and a diplomatic accord on water flow with the neighboring state became an international agreement for flood mitigation. This cooperation measure, though born of tragedy, aims to rebuild sanctuary and learning for the region's children.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0",
          "result-1",
